From e604603f51471ee4a8869606ae9ca0a2a4b24934 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AlexProgrammerDE <40795980+AlexProgrammerDE@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:55:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(resource-packs): select native resources by world
 version

Select cumulative vanilla metadata, licensed images, atlas aliases, actor
dependencies, and audio using the base-game version advertised by
RESOURCE_PACK_STACK. Server packs retain independent priority. Acquire
licensed resources on the existing worker after that version is known.
Keep their provenance outside server advertisements, carry the version
through native archive format 2, and include it in conversion cache
identity even when the selected files match.

Licensed providers and the optional verified classpath bundle supply
resources that servers reference without resending. Validate protocol,
file hashes, bounds, and overlay order. Preserve path case and restrict
accepted documents to the native rendering dependencies. Missing optional
resources preserve existing fallbacks; malformed present bundles fail.

Canonicalize biome identifiers while preserving custom namespaces and
whole-definition priority. Load legacy biomes_client.json fog bindings
separately from modern biome metadata. Honor per-biome inheritance and
data-default clearing without deleting modern definitions or fog assets.
Skip built-in legacy bindings for base versions 1.21.40 and newer, while
continuing to load server legacy bindings, as the Creator reference states:
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/minecraft/creator/reference/content/clientbiomesreference/examples/clientbiomesoverview

Bedrock 1.26.60.5, protocol 2225, native Fancy controls establish lower air
inheritance beneath water-only bindings, replacement falling to the data
default, and legacy precedence over a higher modern biome definition.
Clearing legacy bindings exposes the modern definition again. Preserve
unqualified server fog names: local controls accept them even with an
explicit 1.26.60 base version; remote version-cutoff behavior remains open.

BDS 1.26.60.6 advertises * for ordinary worlds and 1.20.0 for an isolated
template. Matching 1.26.60.5 client manifests confirm all 55 numeric
vanilla cutoffs. Tests cover version transitions, server priority, archive
ownership, cache identity, and legacy fog composition. Native captures
and licensed resources remain private; these controls do not establish
complete rendering or audio parity.
